{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1775685827,"nonce":"KJ2d48cXtlnAJrf2OXkmfL+XoYw=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM767218","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4209995132"},"message":"Also consider the Disable network when offline option for StarLink.","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775760808,"nonce":"p5XcgKkDAqqdljTGNMlTJ35Zh9I=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM77Vcyz","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4216704179"},"message":"## NTP Time Sync — Dashboard \u0026 Checklist Integration\n\nFrom the NTP investigation (#45, PR #46): the operator router now runs ISC `ntpd` with honest stratum reporting. Salmon's chrony monitors the operator router (as a source), BizzyBoat's router, and gabby (as `noselect` monitors). This means salmon can report time sync status for the whole fleet via `chronyc sources`.\n\n### Dashboard suggestion\n\nAdd NTP time sync as a vitals indicator:\n- Per-machine sync status (synced / unsynchronized / unreachable)\n- Offset from reference (green \u003c 50ms, yellow \u003c 500ms, red \u003e 500ms)\n- Stratum value\n\nData source: `chronyc sources` on salmon gives all monitored machines in one query. For machines not yet added as chrony sources, add them as `noselect` entries in `/etc/chrony/sources.d/project11.sources` on salmon.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775763037,"nonce":"JXvqbGosCNaWrspoccv7ylmY6KA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM77Wgt8","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4216982396"},"message":"## Existing ROS 2 Diagnostic Nodes for Dashboard Vitals\n\n`diagnostic_common_diagnostics` (already installed in Jazzy) provides production-ready monitoring nodes that publish to `/diagnostics` and are viewable in `rqt_robot_monitor`:\n\n| Node | Publishes | Relevant Dashboard Vital |\n|------|-----------|--------------------------|\n| `ntp_monitor` | NTP offset, sync status (OK/WARN/ERROR) | Time sync |\n| `cpu_monitor` | CPU usage per core | System health |\n| `ram_monitor` | RAM usage | System health |\n| `hd_monitor` | Disk space | System health |\n| `sensors_monitor` | Hardware sensors (temp, fan, voltage) | Battery level, thermals |\n\n### NTP Monitor Example\n\n```bash\nros2 run diagnostic_common_diagnostics ntp_monitor \\\n    --ros-args -p ntp_hostname:=192.168.13.1 \\\n    -p offset-tolerance:=500 \\\n    -p error-offset-tolerance:=5000000\n```\n\nRun on salmon pointing at the operator router (192.168.13.1) — publishes sync status to `/diagnostics`. Thresholds are configurable (default: warn at 500μs, error at 5ms).\n\n### Dashboard Approach\n\nMany of the vitals listed in this issue (connection status, battery, system health) can be covered by launching these standard nodes on each machine and viewing them in `rqt_robot_monitor` — no custom dashboard code needed for the basics. A `diagnostic_aggregator` node can organize them hierarchically.\n\nRemaining vitals that would need custom nodes:\n- RTK fix quality (from GPS topic)\n- WAN/cellular status (from router API or network checks)\n- WireGuard tunnel health\n\nRef: NTP infrastructure set up in #45 / PR #46.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775765837,"nonce":"92LPFfPTfJ/jrzUZ2uMAe9Etdo8=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM77XcFA","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4217225536"},"message":"## Operator Station UI Architecture (short-term)\n\nThree separate applications, each running independently on the operator station:\n\n| Application | Role |\n|-------------|------|\n| **CAMP** | Mission planning, map, helm control (existing, stays as-is) |\n| **rqt** | Supplementary tools: annunciator panel, camera views w/ staleness, checklist, logbook, radar, UDP bridge |\n| **rviz** | 3D visualization when needed (sonar, point clouds, etc.) |\n\nAll share the same ROS topic space — no coupling between applications. rqt perspective files save/restore panel layouts for consistent operator experience.\n\n### New rqt plugins needed (in `rqt_operator_tools`)\n\n- **Annunciator panel** — distilled status lights for essential vitals (NTP sync, GPS/RTK, battery, connectivity). Subscribes to `/diagnostics_agg` or individual topics. Cockpit-style grid of labeled indicators — all green when fine, lights up on problems.\n- **Image viewer with staleness** — replacement for `rqt_image_view` with colored border based on header stamp age (green → yellow ~2s → red ~5s). Addresses current crashes and missing staleness feedback.\n- **Checklist** — #113\n- **Logbook** — #114 / rqt_operator_tools#1\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775773006,"nonce":"GUb+MpLZvIV1lKpUUZcEU+nfjWA=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM77aXe2","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4217993142"},"message":"## Tide-Aware Navigation — Deployment Checklist\n\nWork from 2026-04-09 produced two PRs that need to be merged and deployed to make the trackline planner account for tidal water levels (fixes the \"start occupied\" issue from the 2026-04-08 water test).\n\n### PRs to merge first\n\n- [ ] [unh_marine_simulation#55](https://github.com/rolker/unh_marine_simulation/pull/55) — tide model, waves, sensor noise in simulator (not strictly needed for boat, but validates the pipeline)\n- [ ] [mru_transform#9](https://github.com/rolker/mru_transform/pull/9) — `chart_datum_node` (ellipsoid → MLLW via PROJ + VDatum grids)\n\n### On gabby (BizzyBoat compute)\n\n**1. Build mru_transform with VDatum grids**\n\nThe CMake build will attempt to download:\n- PROJ geoid grid (`us_noaa_g2018u0.tif`, 16MB) via `projsync`\n- VDatum regional grids (~849MB zip) from NOAA\n\nThese cache in `~/.cache/mru_transform/` and install to the package share (~1.7GB). First build needs internet access. If download fails (gabby may have limited internet), pre-download the zip on a machine with good connectivity and copy to `~/.cache/mru_transform/vdatum_regional.zip` before building.\n\n**2. Add `chart_datum_node` to core_launch.py**\n\nBizzyBoat's `core_launch.py` already launches `mru_transform` and `sea_surface_estimator`. Add `chart_datum_node` alongside them with:\n- `chart_datum_frame`: `bizzy/chart_datum`\n- `map_frame`: `bizzy/map`  \n- `base_frame`: `bizzy/base_link`\n\nThe node gets position from TF (`earth → base_link`), so it needs `mru_transform` running first. Grid paths default to the installed package share location.\n\n**3. Costmap is already configured**\n\nBizzyBoat uses `echoboat_project11/config/nav2_params.yaml` which already sets `global_frame: \u003ctf_prefix\u003e/map_tide` for both local and global costmaps. No config change needed.\n\n**4. Verify the TF tree**\n\nOnce running, the TF tree should show:\n```\nearth → bizzy/map → bizzy/chart_datum  (static, ~-28m at Portsmouth)\n                  → bizzy/map_tide     (dynamic, tracks water surface)\n                  → bizzy/odom → bizzy/base_link\n```\n\nCheck with:\n```bash\nros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo bizzy/map bizzy/chart_datum\nros2 run tf2_ros tf2_echo bizzy/chart_datum bizzy/map_tide  # = current tide height above MLLW\n```\n\n**5. Verify costmap behavior**\n\nWith chart_datum and map_tide both publishing, the costmap operating in `map_tide` frame should now see chart depths at the correct relative depth for the current tide. At high tide, shallow areas become passable; at low tide, they become obstacles.\n\n### What's NOT done yet (future work)\n\n- S57 layer doesn't reference `chart_datum` frame yet — chart depths are still in their raw datum. The `map_tide` costmap frame provides an approximation but the full pipeline needs the S57 layer to place features relative to `chart_datum`.\n- Design doc for the full TF frame hierarchy: [mru_transform#8](https://github.com/rolker/mru_transform/issues/8)\n\n### Known considerations\n\n- VDatum grids only cover US coastal waters. Open ocean returns no coverage — node warns but keeps publishing last valid offset.\n- The PROJ C API needs radians (`proj_torad()`), not degrees. This was a bug that was caught during testing.\n- Recalculation happens every 60s (configurable). Publishing at 1 Hz.\n- First GPS fix needed before chart_datum can compute — node waits for `earth → base_link` TF.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1775773272,"nonce":"zWWVtLRRDGu9vzhHbT8so1LJF5A=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM77afFJ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/43#issuecomment-4218024265"},"message":"## Testing TODO\n\nWhen next on-site with BizzyBoat:\n\n1. **Visual test annunciator** (rqt_operator_tools#3 / PR #4) — try both rqt plugin and standalone mode with live topics\n2. **Apply ISC ntpd to BizzyBoat's RUTX11** (unh_echoboats_project11#45 / PR #46) — same setup as operator router\n3. **Test NTP monitoring** — verify `ntp_monitor` from `diagnostic_common_diagnostics` feeds into the annunciator panel\n\nThese can be done together since the annunciator's default config includes NTP as an indicator.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.6`","files":null},{"type":4,"timestamp":1776364674,"nonce":"tKTxKZ6rgfNI52bDpIAka6OU5i0=","metadata":{"github-id":"CE_lADOK4fCvM7772HHzwAAAAW5CDy3"},"status":2}]}